  "A date, a time or both. It is typed in the order of the locale through a mask, or picked from a calendar and a list of times; `min`, `max` and `disabledDates` limit both ways.": "",
  "Locales": "",
  "The mask follows the locale: day, month and year in its order, with its separators. Month and day names in the calendar, and the first day of the week, come from it too.": "",
  "Time and date with time": "",
  "Limits and validation": "",
  "Fill the mask; the separators are skipped. The value changes once the date is whole and real.": "",
  "Open the calendar (or the times); focus goes to the chosen day.": "",
  "Arrows, Home, End, Page Up / Down (with Shift: a year), Enter to choose — see Calendar.": "",
  "Up, Down, Home, End, Page Up / Down, Enter.": "",
  "Close the picker; with `clearButton` and the picker closed, empty the value.": "",
  "A native `<input>` with its label; the format is the mask the user types into.": "",
  "`aria-haspopup=\"dialog\"`, `aria-expanded`, named from `uiLocale` (\"Choose date\" / \"Choose time\").": "",
  "A `role=\"dialog\"` with the calendar grid (see Calendar) and a list of times (`role=\"listbox\"`).": "",
  "A date that does not exist, outside `min` / `max` or disabled fails validation with a message from `uiLocale`.": "",
  "Button names and messages come from `uiLocale.strings`; dates and names from `locale`.": "",
